      "SummaryText": "EXECUTIVE SUMMARY\n\nThis EPA RMP was prepared in accordance with the requirements of the Clean Air Act \u00a7 112(r), OSHA 29 CFR \u00a7 1910.119, and U.S. Environmental Protection Agency (EPA) at 40 CFR \u00a768. The OSHA PSM and EPA Subpart D RMP standards are applicable to operations at this Facility.  The electronic RMP summarizes the policies and procedures implemented by the Facility to minimize the likelihood of an accident. The electronic RMP also summarizes the actions that the Facility has taken to ensure that a response to a release will be implemented in a proper and timely manner.\n\nPURPOSE FOR UPDATING RMP\n\nTwo Rivers Terminal, LLC is resubmitting the EPA RMP to reflect (1) a change in the Emergency Contact, and (2) the removal of the aqua ammonia blending process, and (3) removal of the aqua ammonia S&H process.  \n \nAlthough the maximum quantity of anhydrous ammonia that is actually stored and handled at the Facility is 230,580 lbs, the total quantity reported in this EPA RMP Report is 495,311 lbs.  The reason for this is because a single anhydrous ammonia railcar (i.e. 165,104 lbs) is counted for the APP Blending, Anhydrous Ammonia Railcar Storage , and Anhydrous Ammonia Storage & Handling processes.   \n\nFACILITY\n\nThe operations at this Facility consist of chemical storage and handling, blending, wholesale and distribution.  One chemical (i.e. anhydrous ammonia) is stored and handled at quantities that exceed the regulatory threshold quantity.  Covered processes operated at this Facility include:\n\no Covered Process 1: Anhydrous Ammonia Railcar Storage\no Covered Process 2: Anhydrous Ammonia Storage and Handling\no Covered Process 3: Ammonium Polyphosphate (APP) Blending\n\nACCIDENT PREVENTION PROGRAM\n\nThe Safety/Manager implements the risk management planning process at this Facility. The Safety/Manager  is assisted by other trained personnel as directed. The Safety/Manager  is responsible for ensuring that its employees are properly trained in the implementation of the"
    },
    {
      "ESSeqNum": 1,
      "FacilityID": 1000121147,
      "SummaryText": "Accident Prevention Program elements as related to their responsibilities.  The accident prevention program elements addressed in the PSM/RMP combined program includes: Management System, Employee Participation, Process Safety Information, Process Hazard Analysis, Operating Procedures, Training, Contractor, Pre-Startup Review, Mechanical Integrity, Hot Work Permit, Management of Change, Incident Investigation, Emergency Response, Compliance Audits, and Trade Secrets.\n\nEMERGENCY RESPONSE PROGRAM\n\nThis is a non-responding Facility. The Facility has coordinated emergency response activities with its local emergency response agency and local fire department. \n\nFIVE YEAR ACCIDENT HISTORY\n\nThere have been no on-site deaths, injuries, or significant property damage; or off-site deaths, injuries, property damage, evacuations, or sheltering in place, in the past five (5) years because of the ammonia operations at this Facility.\n\nOPPORTUNITIES FOR IMPROVEMENT\n\n1. Prepare Management of Change to document the removal of the aqua ammonia processes.\n2. Update program elements that are affected by the recent EPA rule changes, some future changes.\n3. Conduct annual coordination with the local responding agency and the LEPC."
